Mike & Key ARC — Fox Hunt Program

New Dedicated Mailing List

Join FoxHunting@mkarc.groups.io today

Hello M&K members and friends,

We're excited to announce a new dedicated mailing list for the Mike & 
Key Fox Hunt program: *FoxHunting@mkarc.groups.io*


      Why Join?

The FoxHunting list is your central hub for:

  * *Event announcements* — get details about upcoming fox hunts,
    including on-foot ARDF events and regional mobile hunts
  * *Last-minute updates* — weather changes, location adjustments, and
    day-of logistics
  * *Results and photos* — post-hunt summaries, results, and event photos
  * *Discussion and planning* — share techniques, ask questions, discuss
    equipment, and coordinate rides
  * *Build projects* — learn about antenna builds, loaner equipment, and
    DIY projects


      Who Can Join?

*Everyone is welcome!* The FoxHunting list is open to M&K members, 
visitors, and anyone interested in Amateur Radio Direction Finding. You 
don't need to be a club member to participate in fox hunts or join the 
list.


      How to Subscribe

Join the list by visiting:

Subscribe to FoxHunting List <https://mkarc.groups.io/g/FoxHunting>

Or send a blank email to FoxHunting+subscribe@mkarc.groups.io


      Share the Word

Know someone who might be interested in fox hunting? *Please forward 
this announcement* to other hams, radio clubs, or mailing lists that 
might enjoy Amateur Radio Direction Finding activities. All are welcome!


      Upcoming 2026 Events

We have two hunts planned for the remainder of 2026:

  * *Saturday, August 22* — On-foot hunt at Marymoor Park, Redmond
  * *Sunday, September 20* /(tentative)/ — Regional mobile hunt in west
    Snohomish County

Full details and reminders will be sent to the FoxHunting list as dates 
approach.

Questions? Contact *Tom Sayles, KE4HET* at TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com.

More information at mikeandkey.org/foxhunt.php 
<https://mikeandkey.org/foxhunt.php>.

73,
Tom Sayles, KE4HET
Fox Hunt Program Coordinator

